						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#600">The Rules of the Council</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							*** This is an abbreviate form of the rules - the offical rules can be found on out message board.<br />
<br />
General Guild Rules <br />
-------------------- <br />
<br />
1. The first duty of any member of this guild is to uphold the guild's ideals. These are are loyalty, honesty, compassion, noblity, and justness.<br />
<br />
2. To become a member, you must be 20+ and be approved by at least two officers. A reasonably challenging quest assigned by the officers must be completed before becoming a member.<br />
<br />
3. If you are accepted into the guild, get together with another guild member and learn human, elvish, and dwarvish if you don't know them yet. Post your character on guildsay in a timely fashion.<br />
<br />
4. You are to treat all honorable guilds with respect. This is especially applicable to the &lt;Crusaders Reborn&gt; and the &lt;Fellowship of the Wolf&gt;. <br />
<br />
5. If someone is being a jerk, don't retaliate by acting like one yourself. Be calm and reasonable, and if that doesn't work, contact an officer. If there aren't an officers on, use your best judgement and remember that sometimes it's best to just let it go. Kill stealing, training, etc. is strictly forbidden.<br />
<br />
6. Keep the language reasonably mild, and don't say things that you know are going to deeply offend someone.<br />
<br />
7. We don't require that you share your money or items with the guild, but it is strongly encouraged. Your old equipment can make a world of difference to younger players. Be generous to everyone, but especially to your fellow guildmates.<br />
<br />
8. Re-rolling - I believe this issue is still unresolved. There will be some penalties or restrictions for this, but we will take the circumstances into account. <br />
<br />
9. If these rules are not upheld, appropriate disciplinarian action will be taken. If the offenses are severe enough, the member may be removed from the guild. The welfare of the guild takes precedence over personal feelings. <br />
<br />
<br />
Officer/Council Rules <br />
---------------------- <br />
<br />
1. The Leader is an example to the guild. All of the rules of behavior and character are twice as important to the Leader. The Leader should attend to all of the guild's needs. The Leader receives one vote like any other council member and directs the meetings.<br />
<br />
2. The Leader is subject to council's approval. The council may decide to elect a new leader as the needs of our guild change. If the Leader maintained the honor of the guild, there should be no dishonor in this. The Leader may step down to the position of council member if they wish.<br />
<br />
3. A member of the guild is only eligible for the position of Leader if they have served as an officer first.<br />
<br />
4. The Leader may not disband the guild without a majority vote from the entire guild.<br />
<br />
5. Officer and coucil members are leaders - they must attend to the needs of the guild and always put the guild's welfare above their own feelings. They are to serve as an example of the guild's ideals to other guild members.<br />
<br />
6. Officers are not necessarily Council members as well. Officers are subject to the same approval process as any member (outlined below). Officer appointments are decided by the Council and only require a simple majority vote. <br />
<br />
7. For a member to be appointed to the Council, the current Council must agree to their appointment by a two-thirds majority.<br />
<br />
8. Each member of the council, including the leader, will have one vote.<br />
<br />
9. The council will provide at least two raids per month. The raids should collectively present an opportunity for members of all seasons.<br />
<br />
10. The officers will maintain a web page of important quests, useful advice, and critical knowledge. All members are encouraged to submit material.
